  "story": "A 71-year-old man with Klebsiella aerogenes bacteremia from a urinary source is on IV cefepime 2 g every 8 hours, hospital day 3, and still febrile; repeat blood cultures have been drawn and a renal ultrasound for obstruction or abscess is ordered. The isolate's cefepime MIC is 4 (susceptible dose-dependent); no ESBL or ESBL gene was identified.",
