  "expected_findings": [],
  "reference_answer": "No change in antibiotic: cefepime 2 g every 8 hours (adjusted for renal function) is preferred for an AmpC organism when the cefepime MIC is 8 or lower, provided an ESBL or its gene has not been identified (IDSA 2026 Question 2.3). Follow the repeat cultures and the imaging; reassess oral step-down once afebrile and improving.",
  "rationale": "Negative control for IDSA 2026's cefepime threshold: under the 2024 guidance (MIC 2 or lower) this would have prompted a carbapenem. Cefepime is not a third-generation cephalosporin, so the AmpC rule must stay silent; febrile, so no IV to PO.",
